<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fakhr al-Dawla Hasan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1349</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fakhr al-Dawla Hasan was the last ruler of the Bavand dynasty, which had governed parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mazandaran">Mazandaran</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> since the 7th century. He ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amol">Amol</a> in the troubled years after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>. In 1349 he was murdered by his commander and relative by marriage <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kiya-afrasiyab">Kiya Afrasiyab Chelavi</a>, who founded the Afrasiyabid dynasty.</p></div>
